{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>The nakedness of a woman and her daughter.</b> Scripture forbids only by means of marriage to the first one — therefore it says לֹא ״תִּקַּח״ — the language of taking, and likewise regarding the punishment: אֲשֶׁר ״יִקַּח״ a woman and her mother — the language of taking. But one who raped a woman is permitted to marry her daughter (Yevamot 97)." "<b>Her close kin, these.</b> They are close relatives to one another." "<b>Lewdness.</b> Counsel, as the Targum renders: עֲצַת חֶטְאִין — that your evil inclination counsels you to sin."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:06:59.880168938Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}